Intro
Quick, what does this match?
/^(0|[1-9]\d*)\.(0|[1-9]\d*)\.(0|[1-9]\d*)(?:-((?:0|[1-9]\d*|\d*[a-zA-Z-][0-9a-zA-Z-]*)(?:\.(?:0|[1-9]\d*|\d*[a-zA-Z-][0-9a-zA-Z-]*))*))?(?:\+([0-9a-zA-Z-]+(?:\.[0-9a-zA-Z-]+)*))?$/;

// Take
// your
// time...
//
// ...still decoding?
//
// OK, keep reading :)


That's the official regexp from semver.org. It
validates version numbers like:
// matches
"1.2.3"
"0.10.0"
"2.0.0-rc.1"
"1.0.0-alpha.1+build.5"
"1.0.0+20260930"

// doesn't match
"01.2.3"   // leading zero
"1.2"      // missing patch
"v1.2.3"   // no "v" prefix allowed
"1.0.0-01" // numeric pre-release with a leading zero
"1.2.3-"   // empty pre-release


